# Optional. Leave unset and the app derives the API URL from the browser host
# (`lib/api.ts:73`), which is what makes the two-device LAN demo work without a
# rebuild. Only set this if the backend runs somewhere other than <same-host>:8000.

# ── MODE A · UNSET (default) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Works for localhost AND for a phone on the same LAN, because each client
# derives the API from the host it loaded the page from. Requires the backend
# to be reachable on that interface:
#     python -m uvicorn server.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
# Breaks only if the UI is opened through a hostname the backend is not bound
# to — e.g. http://Some-MacBook.local:5173 against a loopback-only uvicorn.

# ── MODE B · STAGE PIN (single laptop, presented from localhost) ────────────
# Removes the hostname failure mode. BREAKS any second-device demo, because a
# phone resolves 127.0.0.1 to itself. Create it with:
#     printf 'VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000\n' > frontend/.env
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ── MODE C · BACKEND ON ANOTHER MACHINE ─────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:8000

# NOTE: `.env` is gitignored (`frontend/.gitignore:7`), so it does NOT travel
# with `git pull`. Every machine that presents must create its own.
# Vite reads it only at dev-server start — restart `npm run dev` after editing.
